rget="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Romans 8:31–39&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#10;&lt;strong&gt;Read alongside: &#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;a class="scripture-card scripture-card--default" href="https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Psalm&amp;#43;73%3A23%E2%80%9328&amp;version=NIV" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__label"&gt;Scripture&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__reference"&gt;Psalm 73:23–28&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="scripture-card__translation"&gt;NIV&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Fear often asks the same question in different ways: &lt;strong&gt;What if I am left on my own?&lt;/strong&gt; What if things change? What if I become weaker? What if I cannot remember what I used to remember, or cannot hold onto everything as tightly as I once did?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The Bible gives a very strong answer: &lt;strong&gt;you are not the one doing all the holding. God is holding you.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>